  "architecture": {
    "Overview": "During the Renaissance in Europe, the Baroque style was born, and that includes artists like Michelangelo, Gian Lorenzo Bernini, Leonardo Da Vinci, Sandro Botticelli or others. Spain had its new baroque style, which built altarpieces with Estípites or Solomonic columns, this style was used to decorate mainly churches, such is the case of the Cathedral of Santa María de la Sede of Seville, the Church of the Holy Spirit La Clerecía  (Salamanca), or the Cathedral of Santa Eulalia in Barcelona."
